            "lens": "review-resilience",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "The new lock polling in engine/review/fsstore/lock_unix.go bounds the wait at 30s and returns ErrLockHeld. An EINTR retries immediately, and any other error such as ENOLCK fails closed, so the blocking verdict is not stored. This replaces the baseline's unbounded blocking flock, so it improves resilience.",
              "The lock is released by closing the directory descriptor on every error path in held_linux.go and lock_unix.go, so no descriptor leaks. Polling every 50ms under contention is negligible load.",
              "lockByPath re-checks the opened directory against the one it looked at (SameFile) before locking, so a swap between look and open is refused.",
              "I found no concrete production failure introduced by this candidate. The other changes are tests, documentation, and a require() guard that fails loudly on an unknown flag name."
            ]
          }
        }
