              {
                "id": "R2-002",
                "lens": "readability",
                "location": "engine/cmd/review_test.go:1183-1196",
                "severity": "SUGGESTION",
                "claim": "The wrapper/engine usage test uses a map keyed by 'engine' strings with inline alignment-dependent literals. Duplicate-looking pairs (e.g. identical key and value for verifier-report) are fine, but the map iteration order is random so failures are reported in nondeterministic order; a slice of pairs would be easier to maintain.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/cmd/review_test.go:1183-1196"
                ],
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 18 changed paths from the provided patches.",
              "Lock logic is cleanly factored: take (shared polling/deadline), lockByPath (non-linux unix), Lock (linux, held_linux.go), and a no-op Lock for non-unix; the unix test set exercises both Lock variants through one table.",
              "No misleading names, dead logic or unexplained constants found: lockWait and lockPoll are documented with rationale, and CHANGELOG, README and usage text were updated consistently with the 30s wait and the platform scope.",
              "Only readability suggestions were found; no defects that hide behavior."
